* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-poop.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|uːp|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
{{uncertain|en}}, possibly from {{inh|en|enm|poupen|t=to make a gulping sound while drinking, blow on a horn, toot}}. Compare {{cog|nl|poepen|t=to defecate}}, {{cog|nds-de|pupen|t=to fart; break wind}}. Also representing {{m|en|poo}} pronounced with the mouth snapped closed at the end.

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete|intransitive}} To make a short [[blast]] on a [[horn]]. {{defdate|from late 14th c.}}
#: {{syn|en|toot}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|intransitive}} To [[break wind]]. {{defdate|from 18th c.}}
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:flatulate}}
# {{lb|en|informal|intransitive}} To [[defecate]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:defecate}}
#: {{ux|en|His horse '''pooped''' right in the middle of the parade.}}
## {{lb|en|informal|transitive}} To defecate in or on something.
##: {{usex|en|You might want a spare change of underwear in case you '''poop''' your pants.}}
## {{lb|en|informal|reflexive}} To defecate on one's person.
##: {{usex|en|You'll '''poop''' yourself if you have to walk all five miles home without stopping.}}

