====Interjection====
{{en-intj}}

# {{lb|en|childish|euphemism}} {{n-g|Expressing [[annoyed]] [[disappointment]].}}
#: {{usex|en|'''Poop.''' The copier's broken again.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Calvin & Hobbes|author=Bill Watterson|format=comic|date=Jul 29 1986|passage=I don't need him for a friend. I can have fun by myself! ... '''Poop'''.}}

=====Usage notes=====
*Apart from the standalone interjection, ''poop'' and phrases containing it may be used to replace various obscene words, either to reach a young audience or for humorous effect.
:*{{usex|en|You realize the machine is all '''pooped''' up again, right? It's not going to work.}}
:* {{quote-book|en|date=Dec 2020|title=Invader Zim Comics|url=https://archive.org/details/invader-zim-comics/Invader%20ZIM%20Vol.%2010%20%282020%29/page/n121/mode/2up|passage=What the '''poop''', Chammy?! Not everything has to be best friends, especially not those things!}}
:* {{quote-book|en|year=2022|title=Good Dogs on a Bad Day|url=https://www.google.com/books/edition/Good_Dogs_on_a_Bad_Day/GbVVEAAAQBAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&pg=PA55&printsec=frontcover|page=55|passage="I'm neither," King moaned.  "I just really '''pooped''' on it this time, and now Erin will be mad at me forever!"|author=Rachel Wenitsky, David Sidorov }}

