===Etymology 4===
From {{inh|en|enm|poupe}}, {{m|enm|pope}}, from {{der|en|fro|pope}}, {{m|fro|poupe}}, {{m|fro|pouppe}}, from {{der|en|it|poppa}}, from {{der|en|VL.|*puppa}}, from {{der|en|la|puppis}}, all meaning “stern of a ship”.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|en|poup|poupe|puppe||obsolete}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|stern}} {{lb|en|nautical}} The [[stern]] of a [[ship]].
#: {{syn|en|stern}}
#: {{ant|en|bow}}
#* {{seeCites|en}}
# {{lb|en|nautical}} The [[poop deck]].
#* {{RQ:Eddison Worm|18|Omens thicken upon us {{...}} Next, the stumbling of the King whenas he went upon the '''poop''' of the long ship which bare us on this voyage to these islands.}}

